  <issue>
  Allow UVA sampling where train_nid/train_eid is provided on the CPU
## 🚀 Feature
For many sampling techniques, the number of input nodes is much larger than the number of output nodes. As a result the cost of copying the output_nodes in a mini-batch to the GPU is relatively negligible (especially since intermediate layer seed nodes will be produced on the GPU in UVA sampling).

If `use_uva=True` in the dataloader, it would be great if it would then copy the output_nodes for the  mini-batch to the GPU before calling sampling. This would simplify the use_ddp workflow, as users could just store their train_nid in shared memory, and not duplicate them across all GPUs.


